Spec: PackageMod

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Sub-command dispatcher for `agent package …`: the developer/CI-side package toolkit —
    build, lint, update, test, validate, unpack — behind one clap group, dispatched
    synchronously with no cluster dependency at this level.

Owns:
  ./mod.rs

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap `Parser`, `Debug`; single field @command: @Commands. Consumed by
    ./../main.rs (`Package` dispatch arm; spec pending ./../main.sdd).
  @Commands — clap `Subcommand`, `Debug`, six variants with `///` doc help verbatim:
    @Build(build::Parameters) doc `Pack a directory into a package`,
    @Lint(lint::Parameters) doc `Lint a package`,
    @Update(update::Parameters) doc `Update a package`,
    @Test(test::Parameters) doc `Test a package`,
    @Validate(validate::Parameters) doc `Validate a package`,
    @Unpack(unpack::Parameters) doc `Unpack a directory into a package` — that last
    help text reads "directory into a package" while the lane unpacks an image into a
    directory (see ./unpack.sdd); the inverted wording is frozen.
  @run — sync fn, takes `&Parameters`, returns `()`.

Accepts:
  A parsed @Commands tree; flag contracts live in each leaf spec.

Returns:
  `()` — success falls off the end; every @Err lane ends in @std::process::exit.

Handles:
  Leaf @Err per arm, Display-only @tracing::error! then frozen exit code:
    Build `Packing directory failed with: {e:}` → 1;
    Lint `Linting the package failed with: {e:}` → 1;
    Update `Updating the package failed with: {e:}` → 2;
    Test `Testing the package failed with: {e:}` → 3;
    Unpack `Unpacking OCI image to directory failed with: {e:}` → 4;
    Validate `The package failed to validate: {e:}` → 4.
  Panics — unwound to main's runtime; nothing caught here.

Must:
  Keep all six leaf mods private.
  Run synchronously with NO @common::context::init_k8s() call at dispatch level —
    leaves that touch OCI or a cluster (./unpack.sdd, ./test.sdd) manage their own
    needs per their specs.
  Keep the exit ladder frozen including the Unpack/Validate collision at 4 and the
    Build/Lint collision at 1.

Depends on:
  ./build.sdd, ./lint.sdd, ./update.sdd, ./test.sdd, ./validate.sdd, ./unpack.sdd —
    leaf contracts.
  ./../main.rs — caller (`package::run(args)`, no await); spec pending ./../main.sdd.

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later whether the 4-collision (Unpack vs Validate) and 1-collision
      (Build vs Lint) need distinct codes for CI consumers, and fix the Unpack help
      text inversion (frozen until reviewed).
  [ ] Cover the dispatcher with tests; no `#[cfg(test)]` module exists here.

Done when:
  Dispatch table, sync posture, and the exit ladder hold under tests.

Scenario: lint failure exits 1 sharing the code with build
  Given `PackageMod` @Commands::Lint whose leaf returns @Err (any lint finding —
    see ./lint.sdd's Ok/Err discipline)
  When @run reaches the lint arm
  Then the frozen lint log line prints and @process::exit(1) is reached

Scenario: validate failure exits 4 like unpack
  Given @Commands::Validate whose leaf returns @Err (./validate.sdd)
  When @run reaches the validate arm
  Then exit 4 follows the frozen validate log line
